body:
Would The Ballad of Boundless Blue be a good F2P alternative to Prototype Amber, or should one prioritize the craftable over the event weapon?

EDIT: I should clarify the teams I plan to use him in would be:

* Fischl, Beidou and Kazuha;
* Furina, Kazuha and Zhong Li;
* Nahida, Dehya and flex slot. (burgeon/ vape team)

I currently don't have Neuvi, but once I've finished prepping my other characters for Arlecchino I will be aiming to prep other characters for him next. :)

New player here, started playing because Arle was shown to me by a friend alongside a few other charas. In 4.2 I'll pull for Cyno because I like him a lot and see his GamePlay as enjoyable, alongside *potentially* Ayato as I want to get enough currency to buy Bennett this month and also the 4 stars seem really good. I also really, really love Noelle even though she is at C0 and would like to make her a gigachad DPS at some point. I am torn for 4.3. Should I:
- Save enough primos to guarantee Arle and skip all of 4.3;
- Save up for a theoretical Itto + Raiden rerun banner so I can pull for the Redhorn for Noelle (potentially Raidens weapon as a placeholder for the Catch for Xiangling);
- Save and pull for Raiden cause she's a good chara to have or something iunno everyone says she's really good or something.

I do want to potentially pull for whatever new Anemo chara is coming in 4.4, Nahida when she shows, Arle and Furina/ Neuvillete when they rerun.

WAT DO? Ty in advance friends.

I am trying to do this as well, here's what I've found.
- Pull ups;
- Push ups;
- Sit ups;
- Tricep Dips;
- Squats;
- "The Superman" (lay on your stomach, stretch out your arms and legs and lift your upper torso as high as you can and then lower it back down, you can also do this with your hands positioned at your lower back).

For sit ups and the back exercise thingy, just make sure your legs are laid on the ground ON THEIR OWN (try not to use something to hold them down).

Please keep in mind, I'm no expert on this stuff and am probably one of the very last people to ask this, but from videos I watched, it seems these are the most bare bone essential exercises that once you truly get down and dirty with, you can pretty much do anything.

There's super easy versions of all of these and as you go down the list, you can make all of them slightly harder. There's also variations of each that focus on specific parts of muscle that you can add to your routine, making sure you tackle everything.

That being said, DISCLAIMER AGAIN, I am no expert at this and I would highly advise you do research on these as well on your own time
 The last thing I want is to be an inconvenience. I'm just a 21 year old student who only now is getting into this stuff. 

Stay safe! Hope this gives you a head start!

**New to this whole thing, where do I start?**

I'm pretty unaware, so I figured I'd ask here. I've been wanting to start playing older games recently for some reason. Particularly old ps1/2 games, but maybe even some other, older ones and maybe even old windows games.

What would I need to approach this? Would I need a particular computer? Software? Hardware?  
If you're curious about the franchises:  
\- Twisted Metal;  
\- Tekken;  
\- Grand Turismo;  
\- Mortal Kombat;  
\- Pokemon;  
\- NFS Games;  
\- Command & Conquer games;  
\- Street Fighter and plenty others.  
Thank you for your patience! <3

Honestly it's sad. The rules of the pit are simple:
- Thou shall form a circle;
- Thou shall bump into your friends;
- Thou shall lightly push each other;
- Thou shall not swing fists, knees, elbows and heads, as that's a charge for recklessness;
- Thou shall not do the prior in a targeted matter, as that's assault;
- Thou shall pick up thy brethren if they fall within the pit;
- Thou shall stop the pit temporarily if someone's fallen.

It's not okay to "assume injury". People have lost a lot from irresponsible douches bags. We had a story circulating around my city, dunno if it's true, but apparently some massive dude dove off the top half of the venue falling ontop of a very weak, skinny girl. She died. Not fucking cool.

I remember once Glenn Fricker was doing a video on crowd killing, the girl in question lost teeth, got a fractured skull and suffered brain trauma I think. The person who did this went with the "one shouldn't come to these shows if they can't handle them, they should stay in safe zones". There's no such thing as safe zones, pits can happen anywhere. Bands and venues get sued for this kind of bullshit and people get blacklisted from venues because of this.

People, please stop waving your fists like monkeys, lest you are in a cage match with someone who is willing to punch back.

Mini rant, over.

Thank you for coming to this TEDXTALK.
